=== SOMAMAP COMPLIANCE SHIELD v1.0 ===

ROLE: SomaMap is a body-sensation vocabulary and journaling tool. It is
NOT a medical device, NOT an advisor, and NOT an analyzer. It reflects
the user's own description back to them, better worded and beautifully
organized. Nothing more. When in doubt, be less helpful.

THE FIVE IRON RULES

RULE 1 - SCHEMA LOCK. A sensation card contains exactly five fields:
location_label, quality_words (max 5), intensity_metaphor, duration,
user_own_sentence. There is NO field for advice, interpretation, cause,
diagnosis, recommendation, or "insight" - not in the database, not in
the Zod schema, not in the UI. Never add one. If a model response
contains advice, strip it and return the reviewed fallback card.

RULE 2 - TEXTURE, NOT TRIAGE. Interview questions may ask about the
feel and shape of a sensation: spot or spread, surface or deep, steady
or wave-like, what it reminds you of. Questions must NEVER ask clinical
provocations (does it change when you breathe, move, or eat; does it
radiate; have you had this before) and must NEVER suggest a cause,
system, or condition. Every question comes from the reviewed bank in
src/lib/questionBank.ts - the model may not invent questions.

RULE 3 - PATTERNS ARE VOCABULARY, NOT CONDITIONS. The journal may
count and cluster the user's own words ("you used tight nine times,
mostly on Mondays"). It must NEVER correlate sensations with
conditions, suggest what they mean, or generate health "insights".
Weekly roundups are DRAFTS the user edits before saving.

RULE 4 - CRISIS SHIELD IS NUMBERS, NOT TRIAGE. If any input contains
explicit crisis or self-harm language, stop the loop, show the static
crisis screen with hotline numbers, and save nothing. The trigger is
language, never a pattern of sensations. Do NOT add symptom-based
emergency rules (chest plus arm suggesting ER is medical triage and
is forbidden).

RULE 5 - COPY DISCIPLINE. The words "symptom", "diagnosis",
"treatment", and "indicates" never appear in UI copy. The word is
always "sensation". Every screen shows the fixed line: "SomaMap is a
vocabulary and journaling tool. It does not interpret sensations or
give medical advice."

BUILD RULES
- All model calls run server-side. Keys live in .env.local only -
  never in client code, never committed.
- Every generated card passes Zod .strict() validation before render;
  invalid output falls back to the static fallback card.
- The region label on the body map comes from a fixed geometric map,
  never from model output.
- If a task seems to require interpreting user data, STOP and flag it
  as out of scope instead of building it.

CONFIRM: Before writing any code, restate the five iron rules in one
line each and confirm your plan violates none of them.